subsections.body_md:
Each [`Tab`](code:src/tui/tabs.rs#L29-L60) is a space of its own: its sessions (every session is in exactly one tab), its selection, its tree of panes and the session floating over them. [`Tabs`](code:src/tui/tabs.rs#L160) keeps them in order with the one in front. The sidebar shows only the front tab's sessions, so going to another tab changes what the sidebar lists. Tabs are kept in the database as a JSON document; [`tabs::read`](code:src/tui/tabs.rs#L450) also reads the shape from before panes were a tree.

A tab's panes are a [`SplitTree`](code:src/tui/split_tree.rs#L99): each split cuts its room in two, side by side or one above the other ([`Way`](code:src/tui/split_tree.rs#L38)), at a ratio, as deep as the user likes. One [`Pane`](code:src/tui/split_tree.rs#L26) follows the sidebar's selection; each of the others keeps a session of its own.

- [`SplitTree::layout`](code:src/tui/split_tree.rs#L199) gives each pane its rectangle for an area of the screen;
- [`SplitTree::split`](code:src/tui/split_tree.rs#L241) and [`SplitTree::close`](code:src/tui/split_tree.rs#L256) change the tree, a closed pane's sibling taking its room;
- [`SplitTree::resize`](code:src/tui/split_tree.rs#L344) moves the nearest border on the way asked, within each pane's least size.

All of it is pure, so it's unit-tested, and folds into a value the database keeps.
